From 19c30f1fa14e9b0c2a795d58ff3706e6bdbe3a26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:19:51 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] CUDA: half2 mat-vec for sm_60 (MMVH)

Pascal sm_60 emulates the integer dot product used by MMVQ. The H1
pre-hardware design measured 3.9-5.5 ALU instructions per weight per
column for the affected upstream paths. The h2 prototype unpacks once
for all columns: 2.63-2.78 at B=1 and 1.07-1.19 at B=8. Its CPU model
found median error normalized by weight and activation norms of
2.2e-6 to 7.7e-6, versus 2.6e-5 to 2.3e-4 for q8_1. These are static
counts and CPU evidence, not P100 performance or GPU FP16 correctness.

Port the block-scaled h16 pre-pass and CHAIN=16 half2 dot product for
q4_0, q8_0 and q4_K at batch 1 through 8. Use 128-bit loads for eight
halves instead of the prototype's 32-bit loads, which accounted for
about 40% of instructions at batch >= 4. Keep one warp per row and
expose rows per CTA in one constexpr table. sm_60 static loop and total
instruction counts tie for 1, 2 and 4 rows, so use one on ties; P100
launch tuning remains pending. No shared memory is used.

GGML_CUDA_DISABLE_MMVH disables automatic selection. GGML_CUDA_FORCE_MMVH
forces selection, including the FP32-emulation path on Maxwell sm_52,
and takes precedence over DISABLE. Both are read once and checked for
presence, including empty or zero-valued strings. Automatic selection
uses the specified cc >= 600 && cc < 610 range, contiguous F32 src1,
and the three supported weight types at batch <= 8.

Exclude non-contiguous activations, MUL_MAT_ID (ids), and every fusion
request; those retain MMVQ. Share one eligibility helper between the
MMVQ entry and graph fusion gate. This trades gate/up/GLU fusion for
the intended faster mat-vec and must be measured on the P100.

The eval suite already covers q4_0/q8_0 at k=4096 for n=1,8 and q4_K
for n=1..8. Add only the 36 missing (type,k,n) combinations for k=4096
and 14336. Keep the existing MUL_MAT NMSE threshold unchanged.

Applies at bench/LLAMA_COMMIT after 0001 and 0002; independent of 0003
and 0004. Maxwell correctness and all P100 GPU checks remain pending.

Assisted-by: Codex
